# Nether Fiend — a Strong enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 8/12 Strong enemies — 22 life, bribe 100 gold
# enemy: Nether Fiend (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0151.dck "Nether Fiend (B, 4th)" [Tier 3 — Manalink 3
#   file dated 2016-02-15; its first 13 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 11 lines (60
#   cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/nether_fiend.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 8)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/nether_fiend.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Strong) — "Nether Fiend" (Original)
#   [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Nether Fiend
20 Swamp
2 Soul Net
4 The Hive
4 Animate Dead
4 Nether Shadow
4 Lord of the Pit
3 Erg Raiders
4 Black Knight
2 Frozen Shade
4 Mishra's Factory
2 Junún Efreet
2 Kormus Bell
3 Xenic Poltergeist
3 Terror
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Terror
#   .vBlack  3 Bog Imp
#   .vBlue   3 Terror
#   .vGreen  3 Terror
#   .vRed    3 Terror
#   .vWhite  3 Terror
SB: 3 Bog Imp
